What is the time scale in the NH?

While fighting one turn gives time
for one strike so it could be something
like 10 seconds of real time.

On the other hand you get hungry and
die of starvation approximately in
10,000 turns which would be
100,000 seconds which equals to one day.

But to die of starvation takes about
a month at least of real time.
This would mean that one turn equals
2,592,000/10,000=259s=4min

But still one doesn't need to sleep at
all in the game. So you die of starvation
before you fall alseep.

And still you can be beaten to pulp
just one strike away from death.
In real life this would mean something like
few months. But in NH you will be back
on your feet in few hundred turns.
 
And still you die of sickness in few turns.
Pretty fast considering that even the most
lethal diseases take at least few days to kill.


So perhaps there is no time scale in the NH.
